      {
        "h_title": "Where to stay in Hat Yai (best area and notable hotels)",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Hat Yai (best area and notable hotels)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 1,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "This guide on where to stay in Hat Yai lists interesting and best-rated hotels in the best area to stay for visitors.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Hat Yai is the largest city in southern Thailand, near the Malaysian border. This inland city is overlooked by foreign visitors who visit the south for the islands, but it’s worth a stop if you are passing through.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Most international visitors are from Malaysia who descend on the city en masse on the weekend and holiday periods, so you will have more competition for hotel rooms if you are visiting then.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "What I like about Hat Yai is that the train station is in the city centre, so you can walk from the station to your hotel. The station is known as Hat Yai Junction, and the city feels like a place that is built for travellers.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "The station is also used as a pickup point for minivans that go to the ports for ferries to the islands. If you are staying near the station then it’s easy to get your onward transport to the islands. No need to mess around with bus stations at the edge of the city.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Hat Yai is famous for the dim sum restaurants, and Kai-Tod Decha serves Hat Yai-style fried chicken. It’s worth a pit stop here to eat your way around the city.",
            "url": "https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1764B9dWVx/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1764B9dWVx/",
                "anchor_text": "dim sum restaurants"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "[Stay in Hat Yai to wake up for dim sum breakfast.]",
            "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DO9uokmE-fs/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DO9uokmE-fs/",
                "anchor_text": "dim sum breakfast"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "This Where To Stay Guide lists the best area to stay in Hat Yai with some notable places to stay.",
            "url": "https://www.nomadicnotes.com/where-to-stay/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.nomadicnotes.com/where-to-stay/",
                "anchor_text": "Where To Stay Guide"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
