      {
        "h_title": "Best area to stay in Hat Yai",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Hat Yai (best area and notable hotels)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "The best area to stay in Hat Yai is in the city centre between the railway line and the Toei River (Mae Nam Toei) to the east. Staying further east of Rajyindee Rd (the large North-South Road) puts you too far from the action for a short-term stay.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "A good aspect about the city area is that it has a gridded street layout, so it feels more like a city and is easy to explore. You can see on the map how there is more activity in the gridded area (the light orange background represents an “area of interest”). Beyond this area, the streets become unplanned and harder to walk around.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Search for hotels in Hat Yai",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/city/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/city/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "Search for hotels in Hat Yai"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Budget hotels",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Hat Yai (best area and notable hotels)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Get GuestHouse 2 (Sangsri 4) is one of the top-rated guesthouses in the city.",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/get-guesthouse-sangsri-4/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/get-guesthouse-sangsri-4/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "Get GuestHouse 2 (Sangsri 4)"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Indra Hotel Hatyai (2-star) is opposite the Odean Shopping Mall, which I would say is the most central intersection of the city. It’s an old hotel that remains popular for its location.",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/indra-hotel-hatyai/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/indra-hotel-hatyai/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "Indra Hotel Hatyai"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Sakura Hotel (2-star) is a big hotel in the city area but away from the main market area. These budget hotels in Hat Yai are showing their age, but they are kept in good condition.",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/sakura-hotel/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/sakura-hotel/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "Sakura Hotel"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Siam Mansion (2-star) is a stylish budget hotel that has dorm beds and private rooms.",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/siam-mansion/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/siam-mansion/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "Siam Mansion"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Mid-range hotels",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Hat Yai (best area and notable hotels)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Hoshi Hotel Hatyai (3-star) is a Japanese-style hotel offering a ryokan-inspired experience. The hotel is on Pracharom Alley, which is showing signs of evolving into the hipster street of Hat Yai with cafes and bars.",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/hoshi-hotel-hatyai/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/hoshi-hotel-hatyai/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "Hoshi Hotel Hatyai"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Sakol Hotel (3-star) is a small modern hotel close to the Odean intersection.",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/sakol-hotel_4/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/sakol-hotel_4/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "Sakol Hotel"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Lee Gardens Plaza Hotel (3.5-star) is one of the big landmark hotels in the city centre near the night market.",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/lee-gardens-plaza-hotel/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/lee-gardens-plaza-hotel/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "Lee Gardens Plaza Hotel"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Centara Hotel Hat Yai (4-star) represents the only brand-name hotel in the city. Centara Hotels & Resorts is a hotel group that was founded in Thailand in 1983, and has since spread to other destinations in Asia.",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/centara-hotel-hat-yai/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/centara-hotel-hat-yai/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "Centara Hotel Hat Yai"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Urbanli Hatyai Hotel (4-star) opened in 2025, and its modern design is a refreshing addition to the collection of older buildings in the city.",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/urbanli-hatyai-hotel-h61737262/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/urbanli-hatyai-hotel-h61737262/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "Urbanli Hatyai Hotel"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Note that Hat Yai is a provincial city, so there are no 5-star hotels or international hotel brands. The Holiday Inn Express Hat Yai is expected to open in 2027, which will make it the first international hotel in Hat Yai.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lantern Hatyai Hotel (3.5-star) is a boutique-style hotel.",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/the-lantern-hatyai/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/the-lantern-hatyai/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "The Lantern Hatyai Hotel"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "V.L. Hatyai Hotel (3.5-star).",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/v-l-hatyai-hotel/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/v-l-hatyai-hotel/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "V.L. Hatyai Hotel"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Here are my notes on Hat Yai from a previous trip.",
            "url": "https://www.nomadicnotes.com/notes-on-hat-yai/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.nomadicnotes.com/notes-on-hat-yai/",
                "anchor_text": "notes on Hat Yai"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Transport",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Hat Yai (best area and notable hotels)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Hat Yai Airport has good domestic connections and limited international flights (such as AirAsia to KL). I have flown from Chiang Mai to Hat Yai (the longest domestic flight in Thailand) and then gone overland to Malaysia after staying in Hat Yai.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "There are overnight trains from Bangkok, and minivans to the coast are timed to meet the trains.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "There are some travel agents in front of the station that book onward travel to the islands. I visited Ko Lipe via Hat Yai, and I booked a van and boat combo ticket in advance.",
            "url": "https://www.nomadicnotes.com/notes-on-koh-lipe/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.nomadicnotes.com/notes-on-koh-lipe/",
                "anchor_text": "Ko Lipe"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://12go.com/en/travel/hat-yai/koh-lipe?z=65037",
                "anchor_text": "van and boat combo ticket"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "There is a hotel at the station ( The Train Hotel Hatyai ) but the city is so close that don’t need to stay here unless you specifically want to stay at a train station.",
            "url": "https://www.agoda.com/the-train-hotel-hatyai/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.agoda.com/the-train-hotel-hatyai/hotel/hat-yai-th.html?cid=1450581",
                "anchor_text": "The Train Hotel Hatyai"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Check Bangkok to Hat Yai trains.",
            "url": "https://12go.com/en/travel/bangkok/hat-yai?z=65037",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://12go.com/en/travel/bangkok/hat-yai?z=65037",
                "anchor_text": "Bangkok to Hat Yai trains"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "I have also taken the train from Hat Yai to Sungai Kolok on the border, and then crossed into Malaysia to get the Jungle Railway.",
            "url": "https://www.nomadicnotes.com/hat-yai-to-sungai-kolok-train/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.nomadicnotes.com/hat-yai-to-sungai-kolok-train/",
                "anchor_text": "train from Hat Yai to Sungai Kolok"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://www.nomadicnotes.com/jungle-railway-malaysia/",
                "anchor_text": "Jungle Railway"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Hat Yai is near the Padang Besar border crossing. Getting the train from Hat Yai to Penang is a much more enjoyable experience than getting a minivan.",
            "url": "https://www.nomadicnotes.com/padang-besar-station/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.nomadicnotes.com/padang-besar-station/",
                "anchor_text": "Padang Besar border crossing"
              },
              {
                "url": "https://www.nomadicnotes.com/padang-besar-station/",
                "anchor_text": "train from Hat Yai to Penang"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "table_content": null
      }
